{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJRTqr4LB7w22xfTJ1w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B4hRaHn26YvuLxjNn2EtZe","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-3VfEdW/memory/partial-refund-rounding-down.md","content":"---\nname: partial-refund-rounding-down\ndescription: Finance rule: partial refunds are always rounded DOWN to the whole cent, never to nearest\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nPartial refunds must always be rounded down (floor) to the whole cent, never rounded to the nearest cent. This is a decision from finance.\n\n**Why:** The payment provider rejects a refund that exceeds what is left of the captured amount. Rounding to nearest could round up, so the last of several partial refunds failed.\n\n**How to apply:** Any code that computes a partial refund amount (proration, split refunds, etc.) must floor to the cent (e.g. integer minor units with floor division, or `ROUND_DOWN`/`floor`), not use round-half-up/half-even. No code change was requested at the time this was recorded (2026-11-26); apply it when touching refund logic.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10360,"cache_read_input_tokens":11962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":10360,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"931719b0-0534-428f-817b-8ba4d887c682","uuid":"37c8b449-1bc6-4811-9195-6b40f83472ce","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:27:07.326Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJRTevbatDwWxtGWw1F","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01B4hRaHn26YvuLxjNn2EtZe":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarken